# FABLE-SONNET-DECL-PREPASS-20260923-137 part 2 (Opus's finding 1): a method
# whose return type is a named Structure used to fail translation SILENTLY
# ("translation failed with no located diagnostic"). Root cause: a named-
# Structure return is stored dt_of_own(1000+foreign) (l2_colon_graph_ty),
# the same as a Structure formal or an own field -- but only l2_emit_formal
# (and l2_colon_bound_ty's own-field branch) recovered the raw foreign code
# before this ticket; l2_emit_sig's own return-type dispatch,
# l2_colon_simple_ty's call-result branch, and l2_prep's call-result-temp
# branch all read the dt-space number raw, silently misreading it as an
# out-of-range foreign index. Fixed at all three sites, through the
# ordinary @: Lmx return ABI (the same lowering a Structure formal or a
# merge result already uses) -- no new rule, no located refusal needed for
# the method itself.
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

# Non-throwing: declare, return, discard the result as a bare statement
# (l2_prep's call-result-temp path, a silent failure on its own before this
# ticket even for a call whose result nothing consumes).
fn: same (Model: x) Model
    return: x
end: same

# Declared-throw ABI variant of the same return type (l2_emit_sig's other
# dispatch block, @@: Lmx l2_out_result -- the same pointer depth
# l2_out_throw already uses in this exact signature, matched by measurement
# rather than assumed).
fn: same_throws (Model: x) Model
    Model: fresh
    fresh\value: x\value
    return: fresh
end: same_throws

# size_t through a Structure formal: the round-trip witness. Assigning a
# call's Structure result into an existing typed variable is a separate,
# already fail-closed boundary (graph assignment admission requires
# receiving-expression tests, unrelated to this ticket) -- passing it
# straight on as an argument is not, so nesting the calls is what proves
# the value the ABI carries is the right one, not just that translation
# does not crash.
fn: check (Model: m) size_t
    return: m\value
end: check

fn: probe () size_t
    Model: a
    a\value: 77U
    same(a)
    same_throws(a)
    return: check(same(a))
end: probe

size_t: r
r: probe()
if: r != 77U
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 90; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
